\f1\fs22 **Month 1**: The cosmic dance has begun. A tiny speck of stardust, no bigger than a pin's point, is choreographing a ballet in the universe of her womb. It's too quiet for the world to hear, but the rhythms of creation have started their tune.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>**Month 2**: The universe within expands. Our star-child is no longer just a whisper, but a secret hum. Like a magician with a deck of cards, nature reveals its first trick, making her wonder if she's really the conjurer or just a spectator.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>**Month 3**: The alchemical vessel begins to bubble. Little fingers, little toes, shaping like clay sculptures under the spell of an unseen artist. Her body - a canvas, now dappled with shades of nausea, wonder, and the early strokes of motherly love.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>**Month 4**: She enters the second act of this play. Morning sickness retreats like low tide, revealing treasures of relief. Beneath her skin, our embryo, now a tiny dancer, taps and twirls, echoing the age-old dance of existence.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>**Month 5**: Her belly, a rising bread dough of life, warms to the touch. Inside, a symphony plays, with heartbeats as the drums and fluid ripples as the strings. The first kicks, fluttering like a caged bird eager to sing its song.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>**Month 6**: Every curve of her spells a story older than time, yet as fresh as morning dew. The world sees her in full bloom, a radiant sunflower in the garden of existence. Our little acrobat, flipping and turning, rehearses for the grand debut.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>**Month 7**: The weight of creation pulls her closer to the earth, but her spirit soars. In her dreams, she dances with her unborn, under a rain of stars. Each Braxton-Hicks, a false alarm, a practice run for the big show.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>**Month 8**: She's a universe, nested within the bigger cosmos. The little astronaut inside floats in zero gravity, touching the boundaries of its space, eager to breach the atmosphere. Sleep eludes her, but dreams? They're more vivid than ever.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>**Month 9**: The final stretch. Every part of her attuned to the signs of the impending cosmic event. Her body, the vessel, prepares its sails, waiting for the wind of labor to guide this ship to the shores of birth.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>**Birth**: And then, in an explosion of starlight, love, and pain, a new galaxy is born. The continuum of life extends, and in her arms, she holds the universe's newest poem, a melody of hope and dreams.\
