<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>**Month 1**: In the vast and perplexing universe, where improbable things happen nine times out of ten, a singular event is taking place inside her. It's a bit like when you realize you've left the kettle on in a spacecraft - unexpected but oddly thrilling.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>**Month 2**: The embryonic being inside has decided to double up, much like the universe decided to have matter and not just void. Oh, and it seems there are hormonal side effects, a lot like a Vogon's reaction to poetry, but with more nausea.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>**Month 3**: Our tiny blob of potentiality is sprouting limbs, possibly trying to hitch a ride to the next big adventure. It's reminiscent of a time traveler who's lost his watch but is quite optimistic about finding it soon.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>**Month 4**: A sense of relative normalcy ensues, if one can call any part of this process 'normal'. It's a lot like feeling you've got the hang of Thursdays, only to realize the weekend's cosmic joke is just around the corner.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>**Month 5**: Movements. The tiny hitchhiker is now actively exploring its current galaxy. It's as if Zaphod Beeblebrox were throwing a mini party inside, complete with questionable dance moves.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>**Month 6**: The exterior universe begins to notice the swelling spaceship and starts offering unsolicited advice. And seats. Mostly seats. It\'92s as if every chair in the galaxy suddenly revealed its existential purpose.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>**Month 7**: More growth, more movement. The reality of an impending new life is as startling as realizing your towel is, in fact, at the other end of the galaxy, and you've been using a very unabsorbent lizard.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>**Month 8**: Sleep, which once was her loyal ally, now behaves like a mischievous Sperm Whale introduced suddenly to a gravitational field. It's there, but it's confused, and it's not sticking around.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>**Month 9**: The anticipation of the great egress is a lot like waiting for a pot of tea made by a particularly meticulous and forgetful robot. You're sure it's going to be worth it, but you do wish it would hurry up.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>**Birth**: After a climax that's nothing short of interstellar, a new being enters the scene. It's a lot like finding the question to the ultimate answer, only to realize the question is "Waaah?" and the answer still is, maddeningly, 42.\

